to be tempted in the wilderness and he was there.

00:26:27.459 --> 00:26:29.919
You can read it in Matthew, you can read it in Luke.

00:26:29.919 --> 00:26:31.519
You read in those two passages of scripture

00:26:31.519 --> 00:26:32.339
and you read about that,

00:26:32.339 --> 00:26:34.839
Mark mentions it a little bit, but not as extensive.

00:26:34.839 --> 00:26:37.459
And you read that and you see that situation going on

00:26:37.459 --> 00:26:39.279
and you'll read this repeatedly,

00:26:39.279 --> 00:26:42.239
that Satan tempts the Lord Jesus Christ, God and flesh

00:26:42.239 --> 00:26:45.559
and Jesus says, it is written.

00:26:46.919 --> 00:26:47.799
It is written.

00:26:48.760 --> 00:26:51.160
And when the temptation comes,

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:52.799
you know it's interesting if you study

00:26:52.799 --> 00:26:54.399
those passages of scripture,

00:26:54.399 --> 00:26:56.040
Jesus doesn't just keep quoting

00:26:56.040 --> 00:26:57.959
the same verse of scripture each time.

00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:01.839
The particular verse of scripture that he quotes

00:27:01.839 --> 00:27:04.859
is the one that is particularly associated

00:27:04.859 --> 00:27:06.679
with the temptation.

00:27:06.679 --> 00:27:08.119
So what do we learn by that?

00:27:08.119 --> 00:27:10.779
Well, we need to learn how to use our sword.

00:27:10.779 --> 00:27:11.619
Amen?

00:27:11.619 --> 00:27:13.480
The Bible is the sword.

00:27:13.480 --> 00:27:14.320
Amen?

00:27:14.320 --> 00:27:16.619
And we read there in Ephesians chapter number six,

00:27:16.619 --> 00:27:18.980
the sword of the spirit, which is the word of God.

00:27:18.980 --> 00:27:23.059
And we need to be able to use our sword skillfully.

00:27:23.059 --> 00:27:25.100
That we can memorize verses of scripture

00:27:25.100 --> 00:27:27.419
that are pertinent to certain temptations

00:27:27.419 --> 00:27:29.940
that we might face and that we can have that opportunity

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:32.579
to be able to quote those scriptures

00:27:32.579 --> 00:27:35.220
in the moment of those temptations.

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:38.339
Because our God has given us what we need

00:27:38.339 --> 00:27:40.459
and we understand that really,

00:27:40.459 --> 00:27:41.799
I said the best way, but the only way

00:27:41.799 --> 00:27:44.399
to really resist the devil is with the word of God.

00:27:45.399 --> 00:27:46.359
And what does that mean?

00:27:46.359 --> 00:27:48.200
It means I need to be a student of the word of God.

00:27:48.200 --> 00:27:49.679
It means I need to get into the word

00:27:49.679 --> 00:27:51.399
and allow the word to get into me

00:27:51.399 --> 00:27:53.019
and then I can take the scriptures

00:27:53.019 --> 00:27:56.279
and I can use them appropriately and skillfully

00:27:56.279 --> 00:27:59.760
that I can know how to deal with those temptations.

00:27:59.760 --> 00:28:01.919
You know, the temptation comes and you say,

00:28:01.919 --> 00:28:03.279
no, I'm not gonna, here's why,

00:28:03.279 --> 00:28:06.399
there's a Bible principle, it is written.

00:28:06.399 --> 00:28:09.519
And this morning, we need to understand

00:28:09.540 --> 00:28:11.700
that there is a principle to follow

00:28:11.700 --> 00:28:13.660
but there's a promise to embrace,

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:16.220
that the Bible says that as we resist the devil,

00:28:16.220 --> 00:28:19.339
that he will flee from you.

00:28:19.339 --> 00:28:20.940
Isn't that awesome?

00:28:20.940 --> 00:28:24.339
I love the imagery here that we see

00:28:24.339 --> 00:28:26.859
in the verse of scripture, that here,

00:28:26.859 --> 00:28:28.980
we find that we are submitted to God.

00:28:28.980 --> 00:28:30.339
It's not because of your strength,

00:28:30.339 --> 00:28:31.820
it's because of his strength.

00:28:31.820 --> 00:28:34.099
It's not because of your might, it's because of his might.

00:28:34.099 --> 00:28:35.539
It's not because you're something,

00:28:35.539 --> 00:28:38.919
it's because he's everything and we've submitted to God

00:28:38.919 --> 00:28:41.179
and we've resisted the devil, we're withstanding,

00:28:41.179 --> 00:28:43.099
we're using the word of God properly

00:28:43.099 --> 00:28:45.859
and the devil flees, praise God.

00:28:46.779 --> 00:28:48.940
Notice, if you look at the text of scripture,

00:28:48.940 --> 00:28:51.299
we'll only deal with part of verse number eight

00:28:51.299 --> 00:28:53.419
but number three this morning,

00:28:53.419 --> 00:28:57.700
the third principle on the pathway to revival

00:28:57.700 --> 00:29:02.020
or the biblical response to worldliness, what do we do?

00:29:02.020 --> 00:29:06.900
Number three, we draw nigh to God, draw nigh to God.

00:29:07.599 --> 00:29:10.400
I put this in my notes this morning,

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:15.400
nearness produces likeness, nearness produces likeness.

00:29:16.159 --> 00:29:19.320
We're to be like him, amen?

00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:20.960
The Bible tells us in Acts chapter four,

00:29:20.960 --> 00:29:24.200
we often quote verse number 12 where Peter stands up

00:29:24.200 --> 00:29:25.880
and says, there's no other name under heaven

00:29:25.880 --> 00:29:29.419
given among men whereby we must be saved.

00:29:29.419 --> 00:29:30.719
The Bible tells us in verse 13,

00:29:30.719 --> 00:29:33.320
they perceived that they were ignorant, unlearned men

00:29:34.219 --> 00:29:37.779
but then it says this, but they had been with Jesus.

00:29:37.779 --> 00:29:38.719
Isn't that awesome?

00:29:40.020 --> 00:29:43.179
Because nearness produces likeness.

00:29:43.179 --> 00:29:46.380
We think about this idea of draw nigh to God.

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:48.099
I've used the same kind of sub points

00:29:48.099 --> 00:29:52.299
as I used in the previous point, it's a principle to follow.

00:29:52.299 --> 00:29:57.260
We sing the song, draw me near, near, near to our God.

00:29:57.260 --> 00:29:58.419
What a blessing.

00:29:58.419 --> 00:30:00.260
You know, it's a huge.

00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:03.240
understanding that we have in our Christian life,

00:30:03.240 --> 00:30:05.140
and it's a huge blessing when we understand

00:30:05.140 --> 00:30:08.540
that God invites us to draw nigh to him.

00:30:08.540 --> 00:30:11.820
He wants us to be in his presence.

00:30:11.820 --> 00:30:12.740
The real question is this,

00:30:12.740 --> 00:30:14.840
how much do we want to be in his presence?

00:30:15.780 --> 00:30:17.200
Draw nigh to God.

00:30:17.200 --> 00:30:19.020
It's a principle to follow.

00:30:19.020 --> 00:30:20.800
We look in the Old Testament,

00:30:20.800 --> 00:30:25.040
we read words such as this, cleave unto the Lord.

00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:27.940
In Deuteronomy chapter number 11,

00:30:27.940 --> 00:30:28.900
and you don't need to turn there,

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:30.140
I'll just read it for you quickly,

00:30:30.140 --> 00:30:33.340
but in Deuteronomy 11 and verse number 22,

00:30:33.340 --> 00:30:34.660
the Bible tells us this,

00:30:34.660 --> 00:30:37.360
and I just love, it's repeated multiple times

00:30:37.360 --> 00:30:38.900
throughout the Old Testament,

00:30:38.900 --> 00:30:40.660
but it says, for if ye shall diligently

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:42.740
keep all these commandments which I command you

00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:45.300
to do them, to love the Lord your God,

00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:49.900
to walk in all his ways, and to cleave unto him.

00:30:49.900 --> 00:30:51.680
To cleave unto him.

00:30:51.680 --> 00:30:53.140
The psalmist says it this way.

00:30:53.140 --> 00:30:58.140
Look in Psalm 73, and Psalm 73 and verse number 28,

00:30:58.420 --> 00:31:00.980
and I love the way that the psalmist

00:31:00.980 --> 00:31:03.420
articulates it here in this portion of scripture

00:31:03.420 --> 00:31:05.540
when we think about this principle

00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:07.540
of draw nigh to God.

00:31:07.540 --> 00:31:08.900
So again, follow the progression,

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:10.700
I've submitted to God,

00:31:10.700 --> 00:31:13.300
I've recognized his authority in my life,

00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:15.260
that I'm not my own, I belong to him,

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:16.660
I've been bought with a price,

00:31:16.660 --> 00:31:18.540
I'm resisting the devil,

00:31:18.540 --> 00:31:20.680
and at the same time I'm drawing nigh to God.

00:31:20.680 --> 00:31:22.380
You know what you're not gonna do?

00:31:22.380 --> 00:31:24.400
Listen, if you're worldly,

00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:26.540
what we read in the previous text last week

00:31:26.540 --> 00:31:28.820
and all that carnality and that worldliness,

00:31:28.820 --> 00:31:29.840
a friend of the world,

00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:31.500
you're not drawing nigh to God.

00:31:33.120 --> 00:31:34.940
You're not drawing nigh to God.

00:31:34.940 --> 00:31:36.860
And so in Psalm 73 and verse 28,

00:31:36.860 --> 00:31:38.300
notice how he says it,

00:31:38.300 --> 00:31:42.900
but it is good for me to draw near to God.

00:31:42.900 --> 00:31:44.500
Isn't that good?

00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:45.340
And he says this,

00:31:45.340 --> 00:31:47.340
I have put my trust in the Lord God

00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:50.100
that I may declare all thy works.

00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:51.540
I would say for every one of us

00:31:51.540 --> 00:31:53.940
that we should echo the words of the psalmist,

00:31:53.940 --> 00:31:58.420
it is good for me to draw near to God.

00:31:58.420 --> 00:32:00.100
Amen, it's good for me.

00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:01.700
I wanna get into his presence,

00:32:01.700 --> 00:32:06.020
Psalm 1611, in his presence is fullness of joy.

00:32:06.020 --> 00:32:08.160
And listen, it's not drudgery,

00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:09.620
it's not difficulty,

00:32:09.620 --> 00:32:12.900
no, I desire to get into his presence,

00:32:12.900 --> 00:32:15.140
I desire to draw nigh to him,

00:32:15.140 --> 00:32:18.000
to come close to him, to cleave to him.

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:20.840
Jesus uses this word in the New Testament

00:32:20.840 --> 00:32:22.880
in John 15 in verse number four,

00:32:22.880 --> 00:32:25.320
abide, abide in me.

00:32:26.220 --> 00:32:29.860
Thinking about that, that drawing nigh to God.

00:32:29.860 --> 00:32:31.880
You ever walk with someone?

00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:34.280
Have you ever walked with someone?

00:32:34.280 --> 00:32:36.120
Sometimes I find myself doing this

00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:38.500
and I don't mean to be silly about it,

00:32:38.500 --> 00:32:39.880
but see, when you walk with someone,

00:32:39.880 --> 00:32:41.080
is there ever a time in your life

00:32:41.080 --> 00:32:43.120
when you're not walking at the same pace?

00:32:44.880 --> 00:32:46.480
Sometimes when I'm not careful,

00:32:46.480 --> 00:32:47.940
I'll get ahead of Holly.

00:32:48.940 --> 00:32:51.300
Now, I'm not saying that she walks slow,

00:32:51.300 --> 00:32:53.580
it's just sometimes I'm like,

00:32:53.580 --> 00:32:54.820
listen, when I park the car,

00:32:54.820 --> 00:32:56.380
like I'm ready to get out and get to the store,

00:32:56.380 --> 00:32:58.260
like I'm not like grabbing six things,

00:32:58.260 --> 00:33:00.220
like let's go, man.

00:33:02.180 --> 00:33:04.000
And so here's what I've learned.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:06.740
I'm not really walking with her

00:33:06.740 --> 00:33:11.580
if I'm way up here and she's way back there, right?

00:33:11.580 --> 00:33:12.860
I'm not walking with her.

00:33:14.100 --> 00:33:15.340
And I'm not walking with God

00:33:15.340 --> 00:33:16.460
if I'm way in front of him

00:33:16.500 --> 00:33:17.860
or if I'm way behind him.

00:33:19.120 --> 00:33:23.980
To walk with him means to walk with him, to abide.

00:33:23.980 --> 00:33:28.980
Now, he's leading me and I'm following him.

00:33:29.220 --> 00:33:31.660
See, you think about the situation in the book of Luke

00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:34.340
when the disciples on the road to Emmaus,

00:33:34.340 --> 00:33:36.300
they're in Luke 24.

00:33:36.300 --> 00:33:37.820
He would have kept on going,

00:33:39.100 --> 00:33:40.820
but they said, come to our house.

00:33:41.820 --> 00:33:43.900
And then their eyes were open, you remember the story?

00:33:43.900 --> 00:33:46.460
And they said, did not our heart burn within us

00:33:46.460 --> 00:33:48.740
when he spoke with us along the way?

00:33:48.740 --> 00:33:50.020
See, because he opened the scriptures

00:33:50.020 --> 00:33:53.220
and he told them all things about himself.

00:33:53.220 --> 00:33:54.700
Praise God.

00:33:54.700 --> 00:33:58.260
And so this idea of abiding in him,

00:33:58.260 --> 00:34:00.700
that I'm walking with him.

00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:06.160
See, sometimes there might be a need

00:34:06.160 --> 00:34:08.520
to kind of slow down a little bit.

00:34:09.380 --> 00:34:10.900
You know that verse that's hard for us

00:34:10.900 --> 00:34:12.660
in Psalm 46 and verse 10?

00:34:12.660 --> 00:34:15.220
Be still and know that I am God.

00:34:17.279 --> 00:34:21.460
Sometimes he just wants us to kind of get into his presence.

00:34:21.460 --> 00:34:23.420
Just abide with him.

00:34:23.420 --> 00:34:25.440
Just spend some time with him.

00:34:25.440 --> 00:34:30.440
I know sometimes we inappropriately apply the truth

00:34:30.580 --> 00:34:33.220
of Revelation 3 when I say it's a fine application,

00:34:33.220 --> 00:34:37.980
but it's not the right hermeneutical principle.

00:34:37.980 --> 00:34:40.180
We talk about the Lord knocking at the heart door

00:34:40.180 --> 00:34:42.140
and that that's a salvation thing.

00:34:42.140 --> 00:34:43.100
It's not.

00:34:44.860 --> 00:34:47.059
He's standing on the outside of his church.

00:34:49.020 --> 00:34:51.220
He's standing on the outside of his church.

00:34:51.220 --> 00:34:52.980
He's knocking on the door.

00:34:52.980 --> 00:34:53.820
Why?

00:34:53.820 --> 00:34:54.900
Because he wants to have fellowship.

00:34:54.900 --> 00:34:56.420
Amen.

00:34:56.420 --> 00:34:57.740
It's his church.

00:34:57.740 --> 00:34:59.900
He bought it, according to Acts chapter 20,

00:34:59.900 --> 00:35:01.500
he bought it with his own blood.

00:35:02.420 --> 00:35:03.240
Amen?

00:35:03.240 --> 00:35:04.080
He's the head of the church,

00:35:04.080 --> 00:35:05.980
according to Colossians chapter number one.

00:35:06.980 --> 00:35:09.640
So you would think he'd just come right in the church.

00:35:10.500 --> 00:35:12.619
But you know why he doesn't?

00:35:12.619 --> 00:35:15.559
Because he wants you to draw nigh to him.

00:35:16.660 --> 00:35:18.500
He doesn't force himself.

00:35:18.500 --> 00:35:20.220
He doesn't force himself.

00:35:20.220 --> 00:35:23.260
And so we think about these truths from the Old Testament

00:35:23.260 --> 00:35:28.059
to cleave, the New Testament to abide.

00:35:28.059 --> 00:35:32.420
The psalmist says it is good for me to draw near to God.

00:35:32.420 --> 00:35:34.580
I think that the psalmist was speaking that

00:35:34.580 --> 00:35:35.960
out of experience.

00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:38.220
Has there been a time in your life

00:35:38.220 --> 00:35:39.720
when you can acknowledge?

00:35:39.720 --> 00:35:42.059
I asked the young people in Sunday school this morning.

00:35:42.059 --> 00:35:43.020
I asked them this question.

00:35:43.020 --> 00:35:44.339
Parents, you're gonna love it.

00:35:44.339 --> 00:35:45.180
I said this.

00:35:45.180 --> 00:35:46.240
Teenagers and the young kids,

00:35:46.240 --> 00:35:47.080
because Holly's not here,

00:35:47.080 --> 00:35:48.140
so I had them combine this morning.

00:35:48.140 --> 00:35:48.980
It was a good class.

00:35:48.980 --> 00:35:49.820
We had fun.

00:35:49.820 --> 00:35:50.640
And I said this.

00:35:50.640 --> 00:35:53.540
I said, do you know when you're not doing something

00:35:53.540 --> 00:35:54.660
with your whole heart?

00:35:56.020 --> 00:35:57.420
And you know what all of them said?

00:35:57.420 --> 00:35:59.580
Yep, I do.

00:35:59.580 --> 00:36:01.220
And so they know at a young age.

00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:02.700
I mean, Camille and Ari, they're like,

00:36:02.700 --> 00:36:05.860
yeah, I know when I'm not doing it with my whole heart.

00:36:05.860 --> 00:36:06.940
Amen?

00:36:06.940 --> 00:36:09.059
Listen, they weren't lying in Sunday school this morning.

00:36:09.059 --> 00:36:09.900
Amen?

00:36:09.900 --> 00:36:10.740
They're telling the truth.

00:36:11.779 --> 00:36:13.700
And you know when you're not near God.

00:36:14.740 --> 00:36:17.700
We might not want to acknowledge it.

00:36:17.700 --> 00:36:20.160
We might not want to acknowledge our backsliding

00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:21.740
and when we're kind of away from him

00:36:21.740 --> 00:36:24.339
and we've drifted and we're kind of living our life

00:36:24.339 --> 00:36:27.660
according to our own rules and I'm being my own boss.

00:36:27.660 --> 00:36:31.000
We might not want to acknowledge that and admit that,

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:34.420
but you know it when it happens in your life.

00:36:34.420 --> 00:36:38.740
You know when you're the one on the throne of your life

00:36:38.740 --> 00:36:40.180
and you know when he's the one

00:36:40.180 --> 00:36:41.940
that's the throne on your life.

00:36:41.940 --> 00:36:44.020
You know when you're drawing nigh to God.

00:36:44.020 --> 00:36:46.660
You know that sweet experience

00:36:46.660 --> 00:36:49.860
and then something happens and whatever it is,

00:36:49.860 --> 00:36:52.220
whether it's just a sin or a weight,

00:36:52.220 --> 00:36:54.740
according to Hebrews chapter 12.

00:36:54.740 --> 00:36:56.980
Whether it's a sin or a weight, something happens

00:36:56.980 --> 00:36:58.420
and there's just a little bit of a drift.

00:36:58.420 --> 00:37:00.740
That's why I say we need revival.

00:37:00.740 --> 00:37:05.740
Revival isn't always because of just egregious sin

00:37:05.779 --> 00:37:08.300
in the life of a believer, though it could be the case

00:37:08.300 --> 00:37:09.700
and that needs to be dealt with,

00:37:09.700 --> 00:37:11.140
but it could just be a weight.

00:37:11.140 --> 00:37:12.500
It could just be a little drift

00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:15.059
where we're just kind of not where we once were.

00:37:15.059 --> 00:37:18.059
We're not in that place of truly abiding

00:37:18.059 --> 00:37:21.440
and having that proper walk with God.

00:37:21.440 --> 00:37:23.540
That's why I said pathway to revival.

00:37:24.420 --> 00:37:26.820
And so we see this principle of draw nigh to God

00:37:26.820 --> 00:37:30.140
and so when I drift, see when I'm drawing nigh to God

00:37:30.140 --> 00:37:33.020
and I know how great it is and I know how wonderful it is

00:37:33.020 --> 00:37:36.220
and the joy and the blessing and oh, this is wonderful,

00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:37.300
but then something happens.

00:37:37.300 --> 00:37:38.260
We're weird people.

00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:40.940
Something happens and I drift and I'm like,

00:37:40.940 --> 00:37:43.980
why am I suffering over here?

00:37:43.980 --> 00:37:45.580
And the psalmist says it is good for me

00:37:45.580 --> 00:37:47.260
to draw nigh to God.

00:37:47.260 --> 00:37:48.100
Why?

00:37:48.100 --> 00:37:50.339
Because he lived life just like we do.

00:37:50.339 --> 00:37:54.140
And we know sometimes we drift.

00:37:54.140 --> 00:37:57.700
Again, a sin or a weight, they need to be dealt with,

00:37:57.700 --> 00:37:59.839
according to Hebrews chapter 12.

00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:01.860
So we find the principle to follow,

00:38:01.860 --> 00:38:04.279
but we find a promise to embrace,

00:38:04.279 --> 00:38:06.440
just as we did in our previous point back there

